<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="@yield('lang', 'en')" data-theme="@yield('theme', 'system')">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="description" content="@yield('description')">
    <title>@yield('title')</title>
    {{-- The pre-paint theme resolver is app.colorMode in config/ui.ts, which
         the framework injects into this layout as well (verified on a real
         status page: the boot script is the first thing in this head).

         It reproduces what this file used to do by hand. `respectExisting`
         makes an already-stamped concrete light or dark authoritative, which
         is the owner's forced theme above; 'system' is not concrete, so it
         falls through to the visitor's stored choice and then their OS. A
         no-JS visitor on a 'system' page still sees the light default, the
         same acceptable edge as before. --}}
    {{-- No <style> block: rule 3 / §11.1. These 23 rules are
         config/crosswind.ts's `statusPageCss()` preflight, scoped to the
         `status` layout group, and every declaration in them is marked
         !important there. That is not decoration: they repaint crosswind
         UTILITIES when the theme is dark, and they used to win on specificity
         alone because both sides were unlayered. A preflight is layered and
         loses to an unlayered rule at any specificity, so without the marks
         the page would render light-on-light in dark mode. --}}
  </head>
  <body class="min-h-screen bg-gray-50 text-gray-900 antialiased">
    {{-- <main> is the stx router's swap target (see layouts/auth.stx for
         the full note). Without it the router found no container and fell
         back to location.href, so the StxLinks between a status page and
         its incident detail — same layout, same 'status' group, so a
         fragment swap is exactly what they should get — full-loaded like
         plain anchors. A bare <main> is transparent here: <body> is not a
         flex or grid container, so it lays out identically. --}}
    <main>
      @yield('content')
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
